{"availability":"available","full":"blakegearin/hex-to-css-filter-library","name":"hex-to-css-filter-library","description":"Library of CSS filters to change the color of an HTML element","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-12-12T08:43:29Z","updated":"2026-10-09T10:25:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.npmjs.com/package/hex-to-css-filter-library","topics":["css","filter","hex-color","javascript","npm-package"],"demo":"https://blakegearin.github.io/hex-to-css-filter-library/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:37.910Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:37.910Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:37.910Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:02:37.910Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A JavaScript library backed by a covering dataset of CSS filters for sRGB: for every one of the 16,777,216 hex colors, the dataset stores a six-function filter chain that — applied to black — renders the target color with a rendered loss under 1%.","Rendered loss is computed from the stored chain itself: black is rendered through invert() sepia() saturate() hue-rotate() brightness() contrast() at floating-point precision, and the absolute per-channel deltas to the target — red, green, blue (0–255) plus hue, saturation, lightness (0–100) — are summed; \"under 1%\" means that sum is under 1. The metric definition, the statistics, and the dataset schema are documented in docs/dataset.md.","Try it live: the demo page turns any hex color into the stored filter chain in the browser."],"features":["Search using SPSA by MultiplyByZer0 on Stack Overflow","NPM package: hex-to-css-filter","Brute force with partial color coverage by Dave on Stack Overflow"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/blakegearin/hex-to-css-filter-library/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"28dc8803ae53cdc34672145dd26617eca65d39cd9b3569f8e88db3adf3a2df54","extractedAt":